## Log Entry: 002 - Test Suite Initialization & ReID Feasibility Assessment
**Timestamp**: 2026-10-06T23:23:14+05:30

### Instance 1: Implementation Details
- **Directory Created**: `test/`
- **Files Created**:
  - `test/README.md`: Formalized benchmarking criteria for local long-footage processing, low-res CCTV handling, and Cross-Video Person Re-Identification (ReID).
- **Technical & Feasibility Assessment**:
  - *Context Memory on Long Footage*: Pure Vision-Language Models (VLMs like LLaVA/Qwen-VL) cannot ingest continuous 30fps video frame-by-frame locally due to $O(N)$ token memory explosion and <1 FPS latency. Hybrid pipeline (YOLO11n-pose + ByteTrack + ReID embeddings) operates at $O(1)$ memory with 50+ FPS throughput.
  - *Cross-Video / Cross-Camera Identity Continuity*:
    - Standard appearance ReID fails when subjects change clothing or CCTV resolution drops below 30px face height.
    - Engineering solution: Multi-modal Identity Graph combining (1) OSNet feature embeddings, (2) Face embeddings (when available), and (3) Spatio-temporal camera topology constraints (handover time windows between cameras).


